: Shared SSE edge-case fixture for the Go (tui/internal/client) and TS
: (apps/core) parser tests. Exercises WHATWG field-parsing rules: no-space
: fields, with-space fields, multi-line data accumulation, comments, unknown
: fields, and id-less events. Decodes to exactly four events, in order:
:   1. id=1 message.created        payload.n=1
:   2. id=2 message.part.delta     payload.text="hi"
:   3. id=3 message.completed      payload.ok=true   (data split across 3 lines)
:   4. id=""  server.heartbeat     payload={}        (no id:, no event:)
: A trailing comment-only block must NOT dispatch an event.
: Keep this file LF-only (see .gitattributes); the parsers strip CR anyway.
id:1
event:message.created
data:{"type":"message.created","occurred_at":"t1","payload":{"n":1}}

id: 2
event: message.part.delta
data: {"type":"message.part.delta","occurred_at":"t2","payload":{"text":"hi"}}

: a comment inside a block is ignored; the data below is split over 3 lines
id:3
data:{"type":"message.completed",
data:"occurred_at":"t3",
data:"payload":{"ok":true}}

retry: 5000
x-unknown-field: ignored
data: {"type":"server.heartbeat","occurred_at":"t4","payload":{}}

: a lone comment with no data must not produce an event

